# TX-F1 (W-TX's fault, writer 10). L §5.19 Booking an observation: "Each end of an observed leg is booked at its place
# from the observation of the version that covers that place on that day"; L §6.1: "Movements stated same, observed rows
# among them, are one movement ... booked once at each place. A place one of them books (an observed row books where its
# statement covers, §5.19) takes that one's legs"; L §5.19 Coverage: the planned movements that touch a covered place on
# a covered day before K are the modelled past, "never booked", and "its observations stand in for it where they are
# booked".
# The whole probe cases/probes/pty/PTY-05 (a joint model over ania and halina, pins over the member files' bytes): each
# member's balance holds the transfer once, +5 000.00 DUK and -5 000.00 DUK (its rows), the family's total 0.00 DUK. snap14
# printed (0.00 DUK, 0.00 DUK).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model pty05
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2024-12-31
  use a = "ania.tally" sha256 "8dbe347296d9ea2d6dc064be191d5d15315f7aefac213b30d1ad6a7c8184634f"
  use d = "halina.tally" sha256 "cd02a45b88b399a845f9bfa800aaa7fab8e6a818405405c891c467a277a79ea1"
  same a.a_stmt[a_g1] = d.gift
  same a.halina = d.acc_halina
  same d.ania = a.acc_ania
  note "PTY-05: the union of two households' statements of one gift, as a joint model (LANGUAGE 6.1). D derives the gift (move gift); A states it as an outside fact, the observed row a_stmt[a_g1] of its own statement. The joint model states that the two are one movement and that each side's outside counterpart is the other's account (same lines); nothing is matched by day and amount."
  note "Rule 2 is the language's own: imports are pinned and never changed, so a member's asks, asked here as a.q, give its own answers (6.1)."

ask q_transfer: count(m in transfers over 2024)

ask q_people: flows(a.acc_ania, 2024), flows(d.acc_halina, 2024)

ask q_family: sum(flows(x, 2024) for x in accounts over 2024)
=== ania.tally
model ania
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2024-12-31
  note "PTY-05, household A (Ania): the gift stated as an outside fact, a row of A's own statement, received from Halina, whom A doesn't keep (an outside place)."

source a_household "Household A's statement: received 5 000.00 from Halina (made up)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place acc_ania: accounts DUK lives 2024-01-01..

place halina: outside lives 2024-01-01..

input a_stmt: observed

ask q_ania: flows(acc_ania, 2024)

version a_statement
  cite a_household
  governs 2024-05
  known 2024-05-02
  covers acc_ania
  a_stmt[a_g1] = (on: 2024-05-02, kind: transfers, leg cash from halina to acc_ania amount 5000.00 DUK) "A-G1: received from Halina"
=== halina.tally
model halina
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2024-12-31
  note "PTY-05, household D (Halina): the gift derived from her own records, a planned movement to Ania, whom D doesn't keep (an outside place)."

source d_household "Household D's records: given 5 000.00 to Ania (made up)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place acc_halina: accounts DUK lives 2024-01-01..

place ania: outside lives 2024-01-01..

input gift_amount: money DUK

input gift_day: date

move gift: transfers
  on gift_day
  leg cash from acc_halina to ania amount gift_amount

ask q_halina: flows(acc_halina, 2024)

version d_records
  cite d_household
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  gift_amount = 5000.00 "D-G1: given to Ania"
  gift_day = 2024-05-02 "D-G1"
=== expect
q_family: 0.00 DUK
  cut 2026-10-25
q_people: (5 000.00 DUK, -5 000.00 DUK)
  cut 2026-10-25
q_transfer: 1
  cut 2026-10-25
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE d.acc_halina is below zero from 2024-05-02
